# MS Teams Network Assessment Report

## Description
This project analyzes network data from Microsoft Teams to assess performance metrics such as loss rate, average latency, and average jitter. It processes raw data, separates it into office and non-office hours, performs statistical analysis, and generates reports and visualizations.

## Features
- Data cleaning and preprocessing
- Separation of data into office and non-office hours
- Calculation of medians, means, and 95th percentiles for key metrics
- Generation of Excel and CSV reports
- Visualization of metrics over time

## Installation
1. Clone the repository:
    ```bash
    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ms-teams-network-assessment.git
    ```
2. Navigate to the project directory:
    ```bash
    cd ms-teams-network-assessment
    ```
3. Install the required dependencies:
    ```bash
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    ```

## Usage
1. Prepare your data files in the [data](http://_vscodecontentref_/0) directory.
2. Run the main analysis script:
    ```bash
    python src/main.py
    ```
3. The output reports and visualizations will be saved in the [output](http://_vscodecontentref_/1) directory.

